<BaseLayout title="Submission guidelines">
<article class="standard-page"><header class="page-heading wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Submissions</p><h1>Submission guidelines</h1><p class="standfirst">Read this before sending work to TSQ.</p></header><div class="gh-content"><p>Send all submissions to <a href="mailto:submissions@thescandinavianquarterly.com">submissions@thescandinavianquarterly.com</a>. Use a clear subject line such as <strong>Poetry Submission — Your Name</strong> or <strong>Art &amp; Photography Submission — Your Name</strong>.</p>
<h2>General</h2><ul><li>We aim to respond to submissions within 48 hours.</li><li>Send work that is complete and ready for editorial consideration.</li><li>Include a short third-person biography in the body of your email.</li><li>Attach written work as a DOC, DOCX or PDF unless a specific call says otherwise.</li><li>For art and photography, send low- or medium-resolution review files or a portfolio link first. We may request publication-quality files after acceptance.</li><li>Simultaneous submissions are welcome; tell us promptly if the work is accepted elsewhere.</li><li>Do not send work you do not have the right to publish.</li><li>For translations, identify the original author and source language and confirm the permissions status where relevant.</li><li>Tell us whether the work has been published before. If it has, include the name of the original publication, the date where known, and a link where available.</li><li>Previously published work is welcome for publication on the TSQ website, provided you retain the rights needed for republication and disclose the first publication.</li><li>Only work first published by The Scandinavian Quarterly is eligible for inclusion in our issue compilations. Reprints published on the website are not included in issue compilations.</li></ul>
<h2>Previously published work</h2><p>We accept reprints for the website. In your submission email, state clearly that the work has been published before and identify the original publication. You must hold the rights necessary for TSQ to republish it.</p><p>Reprints are not eligible for TSQ issue compilations. Issue compilations are reserved for work first published by The Scandinavian Quarterly.</p>
<h2>Categories</h2><div class="guideline-grid"><section><h3>Poetry</h3><p>Send up to 5 poems in one document.</p></section><section><h3>Fiction</h3><p>Send one piece at a time. Short fiction is preferred.</p></section><section><h3>Essays &amp; Criticism</h3><p>Send one essay, review or work of cultural criticism at a time.</p></section><section><h3>Translation</h3><p>We consider literary translation from English into a Nordic language, from a Nordic language into English, or from one Nordic language into another. Send the translated work and enough information for us to assess permissions and attribution.</p></section><section><h3>Art &amp; Photography</h3><p>Send up to 10 images or a portfolio link. Include titles, dates and media where applicable.</p></section></div>
<h2>What happens after you submit</h2><p>We aim to respond within 48 hours. We read submissions editorially rather than by automated scoring. If we want to publish your work, we will contact you by email with any edits, rights information and publication details.</p>
<h2>Rights</h2><p>Any rights requested will be stated clearly at acceptance. Copyright remains with the creator except for the publication rights specifically granted to TSQ.</p>
<h2>Compensation &amp; contributor pages</h2><p>TSQ does not currently offer monetary payment. Every published contributor receives a dedicated contributor page on the TSQ website. The page can include a full biography, portrait, links to books they have written, a personal website, social media accounts, and links to their work published in The Scandinavian Quarterly.</p><p>Eligible work by TSQ contributors is also considered by the editors for external awards, anthologies and annual nominations. Writers, translators, artists and photographers do not need to submit their published TSQ work again to be considered.</p>
<h2>Awards &amp; nominations</h2><p>Work published in The Scandinavian Quarterly may be selected by the editors for awards and annual recognition opportunities, subject to each award’s eligibility rules, dates and nomination limits.</p><p>For writing, this may include the Pushcart Prize, Best of the Net, Best Small Fictions and other appropriate genre-specific opportunities. For visual contributors, we may nominate or enter eligible art and photography for Best of the Net’s Art category and other appropriate visual-art or photography awards and annuals where publication or editor entry is permitted.</p><p>Publication by TSQ does not guarantee a nomination. All nomination and entry decisions remain editorial.</p>
<h2>Questions</h2><p>If a call has special requirements, the call takes precedence over this page. Otherwise, use <a href="mailto:submissions@thescandinavianquarterly.com">submissions@thescandinavianquarterly.com</a>.</p></div></article>
</BaseLayout>
